      "content": "Yes, please. But specifically, I want to see how we can frame the argument that equality of opportunity is actually just a way to mask systemic inequalities. If we only focus on \"opportunity\" and the outcomes stay wildly different, aren't we just legitimizing the status quo? Help me understand why people argue that focusing on outcomes is actually more \"honest\" about real-world impact.",
